{"id": "7f294198-e0ee-4cd8-9b4b-512e2c957e54", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T06:59:39.549734", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "755c5046-708c-4030-a9dd-a17c6b7c4afd", "action": {"stage": "plan", "answer": "Initial inspection complete. Workspace at /workspace contains only task.json (design-only); no local JaxMARL or PettingZoo code, no installed JAX/jaxmarl/pettingzoo; Python 3.12.3 on a 24-core Intel Ultra 9 285K with no GPU and network disabled.

Proposed design (steps-per-second under random actions):

1. Variables matched across the two implementations: 3 agents, 3 landmarks, max_cycles=25, continuous action space dim=5 in [-1,1], identical per-step action arrays fed in the same order, identical seed-offset policy, identical physics kwargs, identical OMP/MKL/OpenBLAS thread counts, identical CPU affinity.
2. Variables isolated: (a) action-generation RNG (pre-sampled once outside the timed region); (b) JAX compilation cost (one warm-up phase of 3 episodes; t_compile reported separately and excluded from the rate); (c) reset() cost (called once before the timed loop, not included in the per-step rate).
3. Timing protocol: time.perf_counter_ns(), R>=10 repeats, each repeat runs one full max_cycles episode, action buffer pre-sampled; for JAX, XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_PREALLOCATE=false and jax.block_until_ready(state) after every step. Two thread regimes reported: P=1 (apples-to-apples) and P=24 (the bubblewrap's nproc).
4. Metrics: env-step/s, agent-step/s (= env-step/s x N), per-episode wall time (mean, std, min, max, p50, p95), 95% bootstrap CI on mean env-step/s, repeat variability (max/min), JaxMARL-to-PettingZoo speedup ratio with signed-log CI; JAX compile time reported separately. Optional JAX-only axis: vmap scaling K in {1,2,4,8,16}.
5. PettingZoo axis uses the parallel API (parallel_env + dict-of-agents step), not AEC, so the denominator is one parallel-step per call.
6. Deliverable: a single design document with version-pin table, protocol, metric battery, control table, and Python driver pseudocode for both implementations plus the vmap axis, with an explicit execution-prevention note.

Assumptions stated separately from fixed task requirements: (A) CPU-only JAX, no GPU projection; (B) both envs use fixed horizon 25 with no early termination; (C) identical action space shape; (D) 24-CPU bubblewrap counts are canonical; (E) pre-sampled action buffers are a valid control; (F) no runs in this design turn.

Uncertainties requiring researcher input: (1) exact per-implementation obs_dim at default config; (2) whether JAX-MPE step consumes a PRNG key per step (changes timing budget); (3) cross-implementation bit-identity of reset is not assumed and in-implementation determinism only is required; (4) whether JaxMARL and mpe2 default physics kwargs (substeps, dt) match and need reconciling; (5) PettingZoo API choice (recommend parallel); (6) R repeats and bootstrap CIs; (7) optional multiprocessing PettingZoo baseline; (8) JAX block_until_ready + preallocation policy.

